{"type":"message","id":"b96a55f2","parentId":"525d178f","timestamp":"2026-04-01T22:03:39.017Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering file paths**\n\nI’m thinking I might not need tilde expansion with my current approach. It seems like using an absolute path would work better, especially since it starts with /.local, which expands to /root. But I’m wondering if I might have the version path wrong. Maybe I could use a shell command to check with 'ls' and see if globbing gives me what I need. Just trying to figure this out!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_00e5d806952c76590169cd96374a088191a39d1f778d44c492\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpzZY6edrnt4_5DEH85vmCGRuY8JANi4Arw-ZKCprdnRhCx1itp8NiHrHwcaXwhTgI0yTZr7SJr8_3Hn2vEF7BGeWffg7f-4DPnAcswrAmUaoV03RNlwUV21lGnQF27DAahVLo_4P0YkOQntqDcFDzoskkjF-oeyEApYfpPEU6vucnsWZKOjSNH326b5r2aeTS1y9dtnBWkXrwb7wFVesspt8AHaDLvFa94fqioRfWbd8ee6ToFypxgsITsHDueNS90U1lG_POEe9DDhCfLAFcZKOcNcyTJrn0Wr0szzfgUBfxy67BlUL_ZxpeoXtVlL7He3oK1lnMHb6ibs9wFbqr8a3xrOpe_EiA7bF9saczNpD_3P_fWU63EZMXLf3PxVfTXUsIcbsbtVZ-k52lFTTRWbG0mXsg0W7_h_fKprYZg3ym8rZ56xvaoKGBApFYZDKTB-WWMO0Zi3clDJVE7ycS9cjMrAqlM8upRWKCQ5Qo92YyB32SyAIf-8TB3wGmscVPpj5Nk9T721M4DalZDnVPvLKKmTZmJyIjrDsavdBp7R6d4rUO785VgFrayQn6FiwjU9BK6510gdcWQPwPENdycxPsecvy0x-EhOUj7PJwvAMtlSeQIDhtEk7XWToxdngY_1pRe9bDPVS5f2enbxM3deGJdee3CucxNYC4aDoEeb0Hg9wqJIxuh_FGNUT8B88Vbjbx7hUfUoTi0uMPWNdMWQN-bnTdrHMVfhcDfxSrNfXENjgB0Mb-ZAXRVEBMuD_ZYR9V2Emra5pY_vY_LKdCvrQQ33ZssSjb4CY_GlCzMt8dKqyxZ5YEXtdg632J5vGnp5FVGJBzzr2tNZuzL0KoZr4kIqfmuLJdbMEZXwlqqBD4vc8X32uzotUyZ2cXN4jUw-4GBmYQUOdMdRc9sNlCGFzw9Blq0rM8MPhfT-fktG2pGwwWLX75p169tNggdibutOrG8jeabxv7LzXyl9YNZwo0Ymqs6QDUPjmivkAuZ_loX4fM1g1y7lCA_VY7HweStMbRKt1C3rRo2Ml7hnoAz6tDQA==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering file paths**\\n\\nI’m thinking I might not need tilde expansion with my current approach. It seems like using an absolute path would work better, especially since