>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.8184036\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d3d34381f68bfaee\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Group chat `/reset` and `/new` commands no longer trigger session reset (Regression) · Issue #25683 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d3d34381f68bfaee\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/25683\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"157cca27fba0f0e0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [Bug]: Group chat `/reset` and `/new` commands no longer trigger session reset (Regression) · Issue #25683 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. # [Bug]: Group chat `/reset` and `/new` commands no longer trigger session reset (Regression) #25683. [[Bug]: Group chat `/reset` and `/new` commands no longer trigger session reset (Regression)](#top)#25683. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. The `/reset` and `/new` commands work correctly in direct messages (DMs) but fail to trigger a session reset in group chats. This is a regression - the feature worked correctly on 2026-02-21 but stopped working by 2026-02-25. * **Previous Working Version**: 2026.2.9 (approximate). * **OS**: Ubuntu 22.04.5 LTS. ### Scenario A: Direct Message (Works). 1. Open a DM with the bot. 2. Send `/reset` or `/reset @botname`. 3. **Expected**: Session closes and new session starts with greeting. 4. **Actual**: Works as expected. ### Scenario B: Group Chat (Broken ). 1. Add bot to a Feishu group chat. 2. Send `/reset @botname` in the group. 3. **Expected**: Bot should start a new session and greet the user. 4. **Actual**: Command is treated as a regular message, no session reset occurs. ### Expected behavior. Please investigate whether this is an intentional change or a regression. If intentional, please document the new behavior and configuration options. If a regression, please restore the previous behavior where `/reset` and `/new` work in group chats. ### Actual behavior. When sending `/reset` in group chat:. * Message is dispatched to existing session instead of triggering reset. * No \\\"New session started\\\" response. * Subsequent `/reset` commands are deduplicated: `skipping duplicate message om_x100b56xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxae7`. Ubuntu 22.04.5 LTS. ### When `/reset` received in group (2026-02-25): # in complete### When `/reset` received in DM (works correctly): # ## Hypothesis # command for`/reset` ` ``/new` ` `****`agent:main:main` ` `****`agent:main:feishu:group:*` `* ` command for. * Multiple bots in same group: Each bot should respond to its own `@mention`. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"157cca27fba0f0e0\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.81133276\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues openclaw \"Apr 1, 2026\" bug regression","provider":"tavily","count":10,"tookMs":3323,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"tavily","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d748e1f7c303bf77\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: OpenClaw v2026.1.30 Skill Loading Regression\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d748e1f7c303bf77\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/8290","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"75e86aa001c67cf6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. # [Bug]: OpenClaw v2026.1.30 Skill Loading Regression #8290. [[Bug]: OpenClaw v2026.1.30 Skill Loading Regression](#top)#8290. Description: Despite a valid openclaw.json and agent.json, core skills (specifically exec and web-search) fail to load. The Gateway initializes the Telegram provider but results in an agent with 0 tools. Skills Status: 7 Eligible | 44 Missing requirements. Plugins: 2 Loaded (Telegram/Gateway) | 28 Disabled. Gateway Status: Exited with reason 1 (likely due to zero active skills). openclaw skills register and agents update return unknown option '--id' or --add-skill. openclaw skills [verb] [skill] returns: error: too many arguments for 'skills'. Manually created agent.json with capabilities and skills arrays. Requested Fix: Clarification on the \"44 missing requirements\" blocking the exec skill on Debian and restoration of CLI verbs for manual skill binding. No fields configured for issues without a type. ## Issue actions.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"75e86aa001c67cf6\">>>","score":0.8740022},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dbffe44903b17466\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: macOS app v2026.2.26 is arm64-only — regression vs v2026.2.25 (universal binary) · Issue #28877 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dbffe44903b17466\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/28877","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c3e18301f36d9187\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: macOS app v2026.2.26 is arm64-only — regression vs v2026.2.25 (universal binary) · Issue #28877 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. # [Bug]: macOS app v2026.2.26 is arm64-only — regression vs v2026.2.25 (universal binary) #28877. [[Bug]: macOS app v2026.2.26 is arm64-only — regression vs v2026.2.25 (universal binary)](#top)#28877. The macOS app shipped in v2026.2.26 is arm64-only. It crashes immediately on Intel Macs with \"You can’t open the application ‘OpenClaw’ because this application is not supported on this Mac.\" v2026.2.25 was a universal binary and worked correctly. 1. Download OpenClaw-2026.2.26.zip from. 2. Unzip and attempt to open OpenClaw.app on an Intel Mac. 3. macOS shows: \"You can’t open the application ‘OpenClaw’ because this application is not supported on this Mac.\". $ lipo -info OpenClaw.app/Contents/MacOS/OpenClaw Non-fat file: OpenClaw.app/Contents/MacOS/OpenClaw is architecture: arm64 $ file OpenClaw.app/Contents/MacOS/OpenClaw OpenClaw.app/Contents/MacOS/OpenClaw: Mach-O 64-bit executable arm64. ### Expected behavior. OpenClaw.app opens normally on Intel Macs, as it did in v2026.2.25 which was a proper universal binary (x86\\_64 + arm64). ### Actual behavior. App fails to launch on Intel Mac. macOS shows \"not supported on this Mac\" error. Screenshot attached showing both the Get Info dialog and the macOS error. macOS 14.8.3 Sonoma (Intel x86\\_64). mac app (OpenClaw-2026.2.26.zip). Release asset: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/releases/download/v2026.2.26/OpenClaw-2026.2.26.zip lipo output confirms arm64-only: Non-fat file: OpenClaw.app/Contents/MacOS/OpenClaw is architecture: arm64 Screenshot below shows Finder Get Info (Kind: Application (Apple silicon)) and the macOS launch error side-by-side. Affected: All Intel Mac users. Severity: Critical — complete blocker, app will not open at all. Frequency: 100% repro on any Intel Mac. Consequence: Intel Mac users cannot run the OpenClaw app; must stay on v2026.2.25 or run from source. * v2026.2.25 was a universal binary (x86\\_64 + arm64) and worked correctly on Intel Macs — this is a clean regression in the build pipeline. * PR fix(mac): default to universal binary for distribution builds #1396 (merged Jan 22, 2026) previously fixed the same issue; the fix appears to have been dropped. * Workaround: stay on v2026.2.25 or run from source (`npm install -g openclaw` works fine on Intel). * The npm package is unaffected — only the macOS .app/.dmg/.zip release assets are broken.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c3e18301f36d9187\">>>","score":0.86331123},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a55c77e7601dceef\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Provider regression — smoke test failure · Issue #47117 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a55c77e7601dceef\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/47117","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"81408124fb81ca80\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe OpenClaw provider smoke test detected **1 failure(s)** across configured models. \"meta\" \"lastTouchedVersion\"\"2026.3.13\" \" \" \"lastTouchedAt\"\"2026-03-14T22:42:43.035Z\" \" \" \"wizard\" \"lastRunAt\"\"2026-03-14T22:42:43.023Z\" \" \" \"lastRunVersion\"\"2026.3.13\" \" \" \"lastRunCommand\" \"configure\" \" \" \"lastRunMode\" \"local\" \" \" \"auth\" \"profiles\"\"mistral:default\" \"provider\" \"mistral\" \" \" \"mode\" \"api_key\" \" \"\"anthropic:default\" \"provider\" \"anthropic\" \" \" \"mode\" \"api_key\" \" \"\"openai:default\" \"provider\" \"openai\" \" \" \"mode\" \"api_key\" \" \" \"models\" \"mode\" \"merge\" \" \" \"providers\" \"mistral\" \"baseUrl\"\"https://api.mistral.ai/v1\" \" \" \"api\"\"openai-completions\" \" \" \"models\" \"id\"\"mistral-large-latest\" \" \" \"name\" \"Mistral Large\" \" \" \"reasoning\" false \"input\" \"text\" \" \" \"image\" \" \" \"cost\" \"input\" 0 \"output\" 0 \"cacheRead\" 0 \"cacheWrite\" 0 \"contextWindow\" 262144 \"maxTokens\" 262144 \"agents\" \"defaults\" \"model\" \"primary\"\"mistral/mistral-large-latest\" \" \" \"fallbacks\"\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6\" \" \" \"models\"\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6\"\"mistral/mistral-large-latest\" \"workspace\"\"/Users/jimmy/.openclaw/workspace\" \" \" \"compaction\" \"mode\" \"safeguard\" \" \" \"maxConcurrent\" 4 \"subagents\" \"maxConcurrent\" 8 \