ctly despite API success Requested FixRestore token usage display in session_status and openclaw sessions output for 2026.3.7+. Token usage information displays as \"unknown\" in session\\_status and openclaw sessions output after upgrading to OpenClaw 2026.3.7. Token usage information displays as \"unknown\" in session\\_status and openclaw sessions output after upgrading to OpenClaw 2026.3.7.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d40ebbc43917fe6f\">>>","score":0.8399576},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9628d2e669ade8ef\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Regression: In new installs, heartbeat runs without guidance · Issue #16065 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9628d2e669ade8ef\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/16065","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9387ffc5939d09a6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: Regression: In new installs, heartbeat runs without guidance · Issue #16065 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Regression: In new installs, heartbeat runs without guidance #16065. [[Bug]: Regression: In new installs, heartbeat runs without guidance](#top)#16065. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingstaleMarked as stale due to inactivityMarked as stale due to inactivity. ## Description. opened on Feb 14, 2026. ## Summary. #12027 removed the creation of HEARTBEAT.md completely---even on a brand new workspace. But the empty template file was intended as a starting point to grow one's own heartbeat actions and as a blocker for heartbeat execution. Previously, in a new workspace, the heartbeat would not run, as there was a blocking \"functionally empty\" file. Now, new workspaces don't have that file, and the heartbeat *will* run, leaving the agent to figure out what to do without any guidance. Removing the file and letting the heartbeat run without it should be a conscious choice for people who change their heartbeat prompt to tell the agent what to do. In my opinion, this is the right approach: #11807 Only create the HEARTBEAT.md on an empty workspace (i.e. when BOOTSTRAP.md is created). ## Steps to reproduce. 1. Install openclaw or add a new agent. 3. bet on what the agent does. ## Expected behavior. HEARTBEAT.md will be created as empty template if and only if the workspace is fresh. ## Actual behavior. HEARTBEAT.md file is never created. ## Environment. ## Logs or screenshots. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingstaleMarked as stale due to inactivityMarked as stale due to inactivity. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9387ffc5939d09a6\">>>","score":0.8296166},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a3051549bf28707f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Regression: 2026.3.13 causes OOM and hangs on low-memory Linux server; 2026.3.11 works · Issue #47430 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a3051549bf28707f\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/47430","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cfcf6c8f230de4e7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: Regression: 2026.3.13 causes OOM and hangs on low-memory Linux server; 2026.3.11 works · Issue #47430 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Regression: 2026.3.13 causes OOM and hangs on low-memory Linux server; 2026.3.11 works #47430. [[Bug]: Regression: 2026.3.13 causes OOM and hangs on low-memory Linux server; 2026.3.11 works](#top)#47430. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingregressionBehavior that previously worked and now failsBehavior that previously worked and now fails. ## Description. opened on Mar 15, 2026. ### Bug type. Regression (worked before, now fails). ### Summary. After upgrading to 2026.3.13, OpenClaw hangs on status/health/probe commands and is repeatedly killed by OOM on a low-memory Linux server; 2026.3.11 works on the same machine. ### Steps to reproduce. 1. Install OpenClaw 2026.3.13 via pnpm global install. 3. Run `openclaw health --json`. 4. Run `timeout 5s openclaw gateway probe`. 5. Check `dmesg -T | grep -Ei 'killed process|out of memory|oom'`. The commands hang or time out, and the kernel OOM killer repeatedly kills the `openclaw` process. ### Expected behavior. The commands should return normally, and the OpenClaw process should remain stable without being killed by OOM. ### Actual behavior. `openclaw status` hangs, `openclaw health --json` hangs, `timeout 5s openclaw gateway probe` exits with 124, and the kernel OOM killer repeatedly kills the `openclaw` process. ### OpenClaw version. ### Operating system. Linux (Alibaba Cloud / CentOS-compatible), 1.8 GiB RAM. ### Install method. ### Model. openai-codex/gpt-5.2. ### Provider / routing chain. ### Config file / key location. ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json ~/.openclaw/agents/main/agent/auth-profiles.json. ### Additional provider/model setup details. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. ### Additional information. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingregressionBehavior that previously worked and now failsBehavior that previously worked and now fails. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cfcf6c8f230de4e7\">>>","score":0.8245895},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"57a79977174e7434\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nBug: Inbound message_id no longer included in metadata (regression) · Issue #17662 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"57a79977174e7434\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/17662","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4e21e4b840705bf3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: Bug: Inbound message_id no longer included in metadata (regression) · Issue #17662 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # Bug: Inbound message\\_id no longer included in metadata (regression) #17662. Bug: Inbound message\\_id no longer included in metadata (regression)#17662. ## Description. opened on Feb 16, 2026. ## Problem. When the system prompt enables reactions (e.g. `reactionLevel: minimal` for Telegram), the agent is told it **can** react to messages. However, the `message` tool's `react` action requires explicit `chatId` and `messageId` parameters. The problem: **the triggering message's ID is not exposed to the agent** in the inbound metadata (`openclaw.inbound_meta.v1`). Meanwhile, `` works perfectly for replies because OpenClaw resolves the triggering message ID internally. But there's no equivalent mechanism for reactions. ## Current behavior. * Inbound metadata contains: `channel`, `chat_type`, `flags` — but **no `messageId`**. * `react` action requires `messageId` (hard requirement in code: `readNumberParam(params, 'messageId', { required: true })`). * Agent has no way to obtain the current message's ID. * Attempting to react without `messageId` → error: `messageId required`. ## Expected behavior. 1. **Include `messageId` in inbound metadata** so the agent can use it for reactions (and other actions like `edit`, `delete`, `reply`):. \"schema\"\"openclaw.inbound_meta.v1\" \" \" \"channel\" \"telegram\" \" \" \"message_id\" 12345 \"chat_id\" \"5494292670\" \" \"... 1. **Add a `` tag** (similar to ``) that resolves internally:. ## Environment. * Channel: Telegram (likely affects all channels). ## Notes. This creates an odd UX where the system prompt says \"Reactions are enabled\" but the agent can never actually react to the triggering message. Option 1 (exposing messageId) would also benefit other use cases like editing or deleting specific messages. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4e21e4b840705bf3\">>>","score":0.82425016},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"87f67e8acced6d33\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Regression: All channel plugins disabled in v2026.2.22 (works in 2026.2.19) · Issue #24395 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"87f67e8acced6d33\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/24395","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6017005a36124160\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: Regression: All channel plugins disabled in v2026.2.22 (works in 2026.2.19) · Issue #24395 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n# [Bug]: Regression: All channel plugins disabled in v2026.2.22 (works in 2026.2.19) #24395. [[Bug]: Regression: All channel plugins disabled in v2026.2.22 (works in 2026.2.19)](#top)#24395. All channel plugins remain `disabled` despite correct configuration. set \"YOUR_TOKEN\" \" \" # Channels section is EMPTY # ### Steps to reproduce #'s the clean copy-paste version for **\"Steps to Reproduce\"**: ' ```markdown ## Steps to Reproduce ### 1. Install broken version ```bashnpm install -g openclaw@2026.2.22. **Output:** `│ telegram │ disabled │ stock:telegram/index.ts │`. npm install -g openclaw@2026.2.19 openclaw gateway restart openclaw status. **Output:** `│ Telegram │ ON │ OK │ token config (...) · accounts 1/1 │` ✅. --- **Paste that into the GitHub issue under \"Steps to Reproduce\"** — it's deterministic and shows the version regression clearly. ### Expected behavior **Expected Behavior:** ```markdown ## Expected Behavior When `channels.telegram.enabled: true` is set and a valid `botToken` is configured: 1. **Plugin loads:** Telegram plugin status shows `loaded` (not `disabled`) 2. **Gateway initializes:** Startup logs show Telegram bot starting 3. **Status shows channel:** `openclaw status` displays:. 4. **Bot responds:** Messages sent to the Telegram bot are received by OpenClaw This works correctly in **v2026.2.19** and earlier versions. openclaw plugins list | grep telegram. │ telegram │ disabled │ stock:telegram/index.ts │ 2026.2.22 │. 2. **No channel initialization:** Gateway startup logs show NO Telegram initialization:. # No telegram, grammy, or channel plugin logs appear. 3. **Empty channels section:** `openclaw status` shows:. 4. **All channel plugins affected:** Not just Telegram — Discord, Slack, Signal, WhatsApp, etc. access '/.../openclaw/extensions/stock/telegram/index.ts'. ## Actual Behavior Actual Behavior ` disabled ` ` openclaw status ` `extensions/stock/telegram/index.ts `. ### OpenClaw version. **OpenClaw Version:** 2026.2.22 **Last Working Version:** 2026.2.19. ** &** ## Environment # | | | | | | |**** | | |**** | | |**** | | |**** |`npm install -g openclaw` ` ` | ## Logs #### Plugin Discovery (Broken) #### Plugin List Output (Broken - v2026.2.22) #### Plugin List Output (Working - v2026.2.19) # ### Key Error # read'/Users/admin/.nvm/versions/node/v24.13.1/lib/node_modules/openclaw/extensions/stock/telegram/index.ts' ' '### Gateway Startup (No Channel Initialization) # \"subsystem\" \" \"\"hooks:loader\" \" \"> \"subsystem\" \" \"\"gateway/heartbeat\" \" \" \"subsystem\" \" \"\"gateway/health-monitor\" \" \"**** `telegram` ` ` `grammy` ` `**** else for ?\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6017005a36124160\">>>","score":0.8194462},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"677426640b81e0a9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Regression: User-configured heartbeat prompt no longer respected · Issue #40255 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"677426640b81e0a9\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/40258/linked_closing_reference?reference_location=REPO_ISSUES_INDEX","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"62026d03845e3efa\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: Regression: User-configured heartbeat prompt no longer respected · Issue #40255 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Regression: User-configured heartbeat prompt no longer respected #40255. [[Bug]: Regression: User-configured heartbeat prompt no longer respected](#top)#40255. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingregressionBehavior that previously worked and now failsBehavior that previously worked and now fails. ## Description. opened on Mar 8, 2026. ### Bug type. Regression (worked before, now fails). ### Summary. 604f22c Adds an additional text to the heartbeat prompt even if the user has configured a different prompt. This may contradict the user prompt, for example one that tells the agent to use the HEARTBEAT.md from the system prompt instead of reading the file from the workspace. ### Steps to reproduce. 1. Set a custom heartbeat prompt. 2. Observe the text \"When reading HEARTBEAT.md, use workspace file ${heartbeatFilePath} (exact case). Do not read docs/heartbeat.md\" being added to it unconditionally. ### Expected behavior. ### Actual behavior. User configuration is stepped on. ### OpenClaw version. ### Operating system. ### Install method. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. Severity blocks workflow, data risk. Consequence missed messages, extra cost. ### Additional information. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingregressionBehavior that previously worked and now failsBehavior that previously worked and now fails. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"62026d03845e3efa\">>>","score":0.8184036},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d3d34381f68bfaee\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Group chat `/reset` and `/new` commands no longer trigger session reset (Regression) · Issue #25683 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d3d34381f68bfaee\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/25683","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"157cca27fba0f0e0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: Group chat `/reset` and `/new` commands no longer trigger session reset (Regression) · Issue #25683 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. # [Bug]: Group chat `/reset` and `/new` commands no longer trigger session reset (Regression) #25683. [[Bug]: Group chat `/reset` and `/new` commands no longer trigger session reset (Regression)](#top)#25683. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. The `/reset` and `/new` commands work correctly in direct messages (DMs) but fail to trigger a session reset in group chats. This is a regression - the feature worked correctly on 2026-02-21 but stopped working by 2026-02-25. * **Previous Working Version**: 2026.2.9 (approximate). * **OS**: Ubuntu 22.04.5 LTS. ### Scenario A: Direct Message (Works). 1. Open a DM with the bot. 2. Send `/reset` or `/reset @botname`. 3. **Expected**: Session closes and new session starts with greeting. 4. **Actual**: Works as expected. ### Scenario B: Group Chat (Broken ). 1. Add bot to a Feishu group chat. 2. Send `/reset @botname` in the group. 3. **Expected**: Bot should start a new session and greet the user. 4. **Actual**: Command is treated as a regular message, no session reset occurs. ### Expected behavior. Please investigate whether this is an intentional change or a regression. If intentional, please document the new behavior and configuration options. If a regression, please restore the previous behavior where `/reset` and `/new` work in group chats. ### Actual behavior. When sending `/reset` in group chat:. * Message is dispatched to existing session instead of triggering reset. * No \"New session started\" response. * Subsequent `/reset` commands are deduplicated: `skipping duplicate message om_x100b56xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxae7`. Ubuntu 22.04.5 LTS. ### When `/reset` received in group (2026-02-25): # in complete### When `/reset` received in DM (works correctly): # ## Hypothesis # command for`/reset` ` ``/new` ` `****`agent:main:main` ` `****`agent:main:feishu:group:*` `* ` command for. * Multiple bots in same group: Each bot should respond to its own `@mention`. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"157cca27fba0f0e0\">>>","score":0.81133276}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775081064030}}
{"type":"message","id":"8cba1e9e","parentId":"bfc19e6b","timestamp":"2026-04-01T22:04:24.100Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_BesXgoYZb2pRYsZ23KZGuucy|fc_00e5d806952c76590169cd96645cd08191a884e8a0758832dd","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull openclaw \\\"Apr 1, 2026\\\"\",\n  \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n  \"count\": 0,\n  \"tookMs\": 2740,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": []\n}"}],"details":{"query":"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull openclaw \"Apr 1, 2026\"","provider":"tavily","count":0,"tookMs":2740,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"tavily","wrapped":true},"results":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775081064065}}
{"type":"message","id":"0183a8f9","parentId":"8cba1e9e","timestamp":"2026-04-01T22:04:24.145Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_j0NEKs7Mo744PnnwfD7CY1dL|fc_00e5d806952c76590169cd96645cd8819183c46200950de954","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues openclaw-weixin bug \\\"Apr 1, 2026\\\"\",\n  \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n  \"count\": 1,\n  \"tookMs\": 1587,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fe9dd0b7ec0b3de1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Feature]: Pre-reset agentic memory flush — /new and daily ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fe9dd0b7ec0b3de1\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/45608\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0fc14d01d0611fab\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n# [Feature]: Pre-reset agentic memory flush — /new and daily reset should get the same memory flush as compaction #45608. [[Feature]: Pre-reset agentic memory flush — /new and daily reset should get the same memory flush as compaction](#top)#45608. Run a silent agentic memory flush before `/new`, `/reset`, and the daily reset destroy the session, using the same mechanism that already runs before compaction. When a user sends `/new` or `/reset` — or when the daily reset fires automatically — the session is destroyed with no agentic flush. Before destroying the session on `/new` or `/reset`, run a silent agentic turn (same pattern as `runMemoryFlushIfNeeded`) that gives the agent a chance to write durable memories to disk. 3. **New step:** Before minting the new `sessionId`, run a silent pre-reset memory flush turn against the *current* session. * The `session-memory` hook and `before_reset` plugin hook (Feb 14 2026, `ab71fdf82`) provide mechanical preservation but no agentic curation.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0fc14d01d0611fab\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.4511578\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues openclaw-weixin bug \"Apr 1, 2026\"","provider":"tavily","count":1,"tookMs":1587,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"tavily","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fe9dd0b7ec0b3de1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Feature]: Pre-reset agentic memory flush — /new and daily ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fe9dd0b7ec0b3de1\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/45608","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0fc14d01d0611fab\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# [Feature]: Pre-reset agentic memory flush — /new and daily reset should get the same memory flush as compaction #45608. [[Feature]: Pre-reset agentic memory flush — /new and daily reset should get the same memory flush as compaction](#top)#45608. Run a silent agentic memory flush before `/new`, `/reset`, and the daily reset destroy the session, using the same mechanism that already runs before compaction. When a user sends `/new` or `/reset` — or when the daily reset fires automatically — the session is destroyed with no agentic flush. Before destroying the session on `/new` or `/reset`, run a silent agentic turn (same pattern as `runMemoryFlushIfNeeded`) that gives the agent a chance to write durable memories to disk. 3. **New step:** Before minting the new `sessionId`, run a silent pre-reset memory flush turn against the *current* session. * The `session-memory` hook and `before_reset` plugin hook (Feb 14 2026, `ab71fdf82`) provide mechanical preservation but no agentic curation.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0fc14d01d0611fab\">>>","score":0.4511578}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775081064100}}
